      "section": "airport (transport noun)",
      "text": "Airport is a compound of air, referring here to aircraft, and port. The word became established for air-transport facilities in the early twentieth century. The formation extends the idea of a transport arrival and departure place to aviation; it does not claim that every airport is a seaport.",
